    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Trailing time-window aggregates per key (count, sum, mean, min, max, distinct) for several windows, such as transactions per card in the last 24 hours.",
    "category": "Preparation",
    "subcategory": "Window",
    "tags": [
        "rolling window",
        "time window",
        "velocity",
        "fraud features",
        "moving aggregate",
        "feature engineering",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "For every row, aggregates the rows of the **same key** within a **trailing time window** ending at its timestamp: transactions in the last 24 hours per card, orders in the last 30 days per customer, alarms in the last hour per machine.\n\n- Windows are measured in **time**, not rows, so irregular data is handled correctly; several windows at once (`1h, 24h, 7d, 30d`)\n- Per window: **count**, **sum**, **mean**, **minimum** and **maximum** of a value, and **distinct** values of another field (for example distinct merchants)\n- Include or exclude the current row (excluded is typical for fraud and velocity features)\n\nMulti-Row Formula covers windows of a fixed number of rows; this block covers windows of a fixed length of time. Minimum, maximum and distinct counts are computed for keys with up to 50,000 rows.",
